@page "/faq"

<PageTitle>FAQ – ScheduleMeister</PageTitle>

<div class="faq-wrapper">
    <div class="faq-header">
        <h2 class="faq-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <p class="faq-subtitle">Everything you need to know about using ScheduleMeister.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
        <h5 class="faq-section-title">📅 Calendar &amp; Schedules</h5>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I view my schedule?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Log in and click <strong>Calendar</strong> in the navigation menu. Your default schedule is loaded automatically. Use the schedule dropdown at the top of the calendar to switch between schedules.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I switch between Week and Month view?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Use the <strong>Week</strong> and <strong>Month</strong> toggle buttons at the top of the calendar. Week view shows a detailed day-by-day layout, while Month view gives a broader overview.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I navigate between months or weeks?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Use the <strong>‹</strong> and <strong>›</strong> arrow buttons to move backward or forward by one week or month at a time.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I filter what is shown on the calendar?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Use the <strong>Work items</strong>, <strong>Absences</strong>, and <strong>Reminders</strong> toggle buttons at the top of the calendar to show or hide each event type.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
        <h5 class="faq-section-title">🗂 Managing Schedules</h5>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I create a new schedule?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Go to <strong>Manage</strong> and click <strong>+ New Schedule</strong>. Give it a name, an optional description, and choose whether it should be the default. Click <strong>Save</strong> to create it.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">What is the default schedule?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">The default schedule is the one automatically loaded when you open the Calendar. You can change the default at any time by clicking <strong>Set Default</strong> next to a schedule on the Manage page.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">Can I have multiple schedules?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Yes. You can create as many schedules as you need — for example, one per month or one per location. Switch between them using the dropdown at the top of the Calendar page.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I delete a schedule?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">On the <strong>Manage</strong> page, click <strong>Delete</strong> next to the schedule and confirm. You cannot delete your only remaining schedule. Its WorkItems, absences, and reminders are permanently deleted before the schedule. If cleanup fails, the schedule is not deleted and an error is shown; data already deleted earlier in the cleanup is not restored.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
        <h5 class="faq-section-title">🔁 Work Item Templates (Managers)</h5>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">What is a Work Item Template?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">A Work Item Template is a reusable work item template that can be made available to one or more schedules. It defines the work items for each day of the week and can be applied to a date range on the Calendar.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I create or edit a Work Item Template?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">On the <strong>Manage</strong> page, find the <strong>Work Item Templates</strong> section below Schedules and click <strong>+ New Work Item Template</strong>. Enter a name, choose at least one available schedule, and add WorkItems by clicking a day. Use <strong>Edit</strong> to change an existing Work Item Template.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">Can a Work Item Template be used on more than one schedule?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Yes. In the Work Item Template editor, select every schedule that should be allowed to use that Work Item Template. On the Calendar, only Work Item Templates enabled for the selected schedule are offered.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I apply a Work Item Template?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">On the <strong>Calendar</strong>, select a schedule and choose an available Work Item Template from <strong>Apply Template</strong>. Choose the date range in the day dialog, or select multiple days and use the multi-day template controls, then apply it. The template creates calendar WorkItems on the selected dates.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">What happens when I delete a Work Item Template?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">On the <strong>Manage</strong> page, click <strong>Delete</strong> next to the Work Item Template and confirm. The Work Item Template and its template WorkItems are deleted. Calendar WorkItems that were already created by applying the Work Item Template are not deleted.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
        <h5 class="faq-section-title">⚙️ Automatic Work Item Assignment (Managers)</h5>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How does automatic assignment work?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
                When you run auto-assign from the Calendar, ScheduleMeister processes only unassigned WorkItems in the selected date range or selected days. It groups them by date and required team member type, orders groups by date and earliest start time, and considers WorkItems within each group by start time:
                <ol>
                    <li>It checks the WorkItem's required team member type against the linked team's workers' primary types.</li>
                    <li>For each WorkItem, it considers matching workers in priority order and assigns it to the first worker who passes the applicable availability, absence, hours, and scheduling checks.</li>
                    <li>After each assignment, it updates that worker's hours and schedule before considering the next WorkItem.</li>
                    <li>If additional-role coverage is enabled, it makes another pass over WorkItems still unassigned, using workers qualified for the required type as an additional role.</li>
                </ol>
                WorkItems that have no eligible worker are left unassigned; auto-assign does not change WorkItems that already have an assignee.
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How are workers prioritized?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Workers with a higher <strong>Work Item Assignment Priority</strong> are considered before lower-priority workers. Workers at the same priority are assigned WorkItems in round-robin order: the starting order is based on display name, then the order rotates after each successful assignment. If a worker is not eligible for a WorkItem, the next worker in that priority group is tried. Lower-priority workers are considered only when no worker in the higher-priority group is eligible. Managers can set each worker's priority from the worker details on the <strong>Manage</strong> page.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">What makes a worker eligible for a WorkItem?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">
                The worker must have a matching primary team member type, or be qualified for that type through additional-role coverage. The <strong>Auto Assign Settings</strong> on the <strong>Manage</strong> page control these checks:
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Availability:</strong> By default, the entire WorkItem must fit within one of the worker's saved availability windows for that day.</li>
                    <li><strong>Approved absences:</strong> By default, an approved absence that overlaps any part of the WorkItem blocks assignment. Pending or denied absences do not block it.</li>
                    <li><strong>Weekly hours:</strong> By default, the worker's existing assigned hours and new assignments are counted against their maximum for a Sunday-to-Saturday week. A maximum of 0 means no weekly cap.</li>
                    <li><strong>WorkItems per day:</strong> By default, a worker can receive at most one WorkItem per day. Turn on <strong>Allow multiple work items per worker per day</strong> to allow more; WorkItems that overlap in time are always blocked.</li>
                </ul>
                Managers can turn off the availability, approved-absence, or weekly-hours checks in Auto Assign Settings. The no-overlapping-WorkItems check always applies.
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How does additional-role coverage work?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">A manager can give a worker additional qualified team member types from that worker's details on the <strong>Manage</strong> page. Additional-role coverage is enabled by default and, by default, is used only after workers with the required type as their primary type have been considered. Turn off <strong>Run additional qualified-role coverage only after primary-role assignment</strong> to include additional-role workers when retrying any WorkItems still unassigned after the primary-role pass. Priority and eligibility rules still apply.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
        <h5 class="faq-section-title">🕐 Work items</h5>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I add a work item?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Click any day on the calendar to open the event modal, switch to the <strong>Work item</strong> tab, fill in the start time, end time, team member type, and any notes, then click <strong>Save work item</strong>.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">Can I assign a work item to a specific employee?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Yes. When creating or editing a WorkItem, use the <strong>Assign To</strong> dropdown to pick a linked team member. The WorkItem will then appear attributed to that employee on the calendar.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">Can I create a recurring work item?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Yes. When adding a WorkItem, choose a <strong>Repeat</strong> option — Daily, Work Week (Mon–Fri), or Weekends — and ScheduleMeister will create one WorkItem for every matching day in that month.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I edit or delete a work item?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Click the WorkItem card on the calendar to open it for editing. Update any fields and click <strong>Save Changes</strong>, or click <strong>Delete</strong> to remove just that occurrence. For recurring WorkItems, you can also delete the entire series at once.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
        <h5 class="faq-section-title">🙅 Absences</h5>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I request an absence?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Click a day on the calendar, switch to the <strong>Absence</strong> tab, enter the absence details and duration, and click <strong>Save</strong>. The request is submitted as pending approval for your manager.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">Can I request a part-day absence?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Yes. When creating a single-day absence, tick the <strong>Part Day</strong> checkbox and enter the start and end times for the partial absence.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I know if my absence has been approved?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Absence cards on the calendar display a coloured badge — <strong>Pending</strong> (grey), <strong>Approved</strong> (green), or <strong>Denied</strong> (red) — so you can see the status at a glance.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How does a manager approve or deny an absence? (Managers)</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Go to the <strong>Manage</strong> page and select a team member from the Team Members panel. Their upcoming absences are listed on the right. Click any absence to open it, change the approval state using the dropdown, and click <strong>Save</strong>.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
        <h5 class="faq-section-title">🔔 Reminders</h5>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I add a reminder?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Click a day on the calendar, switch to the <strong>Reminder</strong> tab, enter a title, choose a colour, add optional notes, and click <strong>Save</strong>. Team leaders can choose a linked team member in the <strong>For</strong> field; otherwise the reminder is for the current user. Reminder visibility follows the team leader/team calendar and assigned user.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">What do the reminder colours mean?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Colours are purely for your own organisation — use them however you like, for example red for urgent items and blue for informational notes.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I edit or delete a reminder?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Click the reminder on the calendar to open the edit form. Update any field and click <strong>Save Changes</strong>, or click <strong>Delete</strong> to remove it.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
        <h5 class="faq-section-title">👥 Team Members (Team Leaders)</h5>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do team members join my team?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Share your <strong>Team Code</strong> with your team members — they can find the join field on their <strong>Account</strong> page. Once they enter the code, they will appear in your Team Members panel on the Manage page.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">Where do I find my Team Code?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Go to the <strong>Manage</strong> page. Your Team Code is displayed in the Team Code section and can be copied to share with employees.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I change a team member's team member type?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">On the <strong>Manage</strong> page, select the team member from the Team Members list. Use the <strong>Team Member Type</strong> dropdown to pick the new role and click <strong>Save</strong>.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">Can I see a team member's availability?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Yes. Select any team member on the Manage page and their <strong>Weekly Availability</strong> is shown in the detail panel, displaying the days and time windows they have set on their own Account page.</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="faq-section">
        <h5 class="faq-section-title">🔐 Account</h5>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I set my availability?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Go to the <strong>Account</strong> page and use the Weekly Availability section to add time windows for each day of the week. Your team leader can view this to help plan WorkItems around your schedule.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I join a team leader's team?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Ask your team leader for their <strong>Team Code</strong>, then enter it in the <strong>Join a Team</strong> field on your Account page and click <strong>Join</strong>.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How long does my login session last?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Your session lasts <strong>8 hours</strong> from the time you log in. After that you will be asked to sign in again.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-item">
            <div class="faq-question">How do I log out?</div>
            <div class="faq-answer">Click the <strong>Logout</strong> link in the navigation menu.</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
